From 625587956dda81973fcc577530b8b5f1deccc69e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vegetableleaf <benzhu2029@u.northwestern.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:37:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CF-CLONE: a clone's copy of a spawner buff carries the
 spawner as the original left it

A Clone's copy of a buff instance now takes the instance's spawner with its other counters: the
timer, the firings of its wave and the firings it has left. The refusal "is cloned carrying ...,
whose spawner's copy is not modelled" is gone.

So the evolved Skeleton's SkeletonDuplication_EV1, fired on the buff visit after the hit, is spent
on the copy and its clone makes nothing; an instance listed by a hit and not yet visited fires on
the clone too, whose child is a clone. On 16.635 data the row is NotCloned, so the copy is taken off
as the clone is made, before any visit.

The copy taking the spawner's state, rather than a fresh spawner from the row, is not traced from
the client: it follows the copy taking every other counter of the instance (hitCounter among them).

BattleSkeletonsEvoTest: a Clone after the first child (a spent copy listed, no child from the clone)
and the same with the row NotCloned (the copy taken off).
